<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="pvp-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/pvpcurrency-conquest-horde.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Conquest and Honor Gear for Discipline Priests</span></h2>While you'll farm most of your pre-raid gear from PVE sources like dungeons, you're also able to buy some PVP items with Conquest Points. You don't need to be good at PVP to earn these and you'll get two epic 483 pieces for your work. If you decide on this path then buy <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=84928/malevolent-gladiators-mooncloth-mantle">
<img alt="Malevolent Gladiator's Mooncloth Mantle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_cloth_raidpriest_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malevolent Gladiator's Mooncloth Mantle</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=84883/malevolent-gladiators-mooncloth-leggings">
<img alt="Malevolent Gladiator's Mooncloth Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pant_cloth_raidpriest_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malevolent Gladiator's Mooncloth Leggings</span></a>. You don't need to worry about the socket bonuses since PVP Power doesn't do anything in PVE. While farming conquest you can also spend the Honor Points you earn on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=84353/dreadful-gladiators-cord-of-cruelty">
<img alt="Dreadful Gladiator's Cord of Cruelty" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_robe_pvpmage_e_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadful Gladiator's Cord of Cruelty</span></a> which is a slight improvement over PVE belts due to its socket.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best World Drop Items for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Mists of Pandaria brings with it a whole lot of world content with the chance to get powerful gear. This includes Rare Mobs, like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50350/morgrinn-crackfang">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Morgrinn Crackfang</span></a>, but also World Bosses such as <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=60491/sha-of-anger">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sha of Anger</span></a>.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="sha-of-anger">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/sha_spell_fire_felfirenova.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Sha of Anger</span></h3>Sha of Anger is notable in that it drops item level 496 Tier 14 Legs and Gloves, as well as various item level 483 Malevolent Gladiator's pieces. This is a great way to get a headstart on your Tier set if you get lucky, but you only get one chance a week so it won't be a big part of your early gearing strategy.<br/>
<br/>The first time you kill the Sha of Anger, it will also drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89317/claw-of-anger">
<img alt="Claw of Anger" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_hand_1h_shaclaw.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Claw of Anger</span></a>. This can be turned in for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90911/furyheart-treads">
<img alt="Furyheart Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Furyheart Treads</span></a>, a strong pair of early Boots.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="rare-mobs">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Rare Mobs</span></h3>There are a lot of Rare mobs scattered around Pandaria, and each one has its own unique drop. Most of these are toys, cosmetics, or similar items, but a small handful can drop gear. These can be useful for getting started at level 90 but you'll replace them quickly.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50340/gaarn-the-toxic">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gaarn the Toxic</span></a> drops <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90725/gaarns-leggings-of-infestation">
<img alt="Gaarn's Leggings of Infestation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaarn's Leggings of Infestation</span></a>, ilvl 440 Pants.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50750/aethis">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Aethis</span></a> drops <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87649/pool-stirrer">
<img alt="Pool-Stirrer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_pandung_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pool-Stirrer</span></a>, an ilvl 420 1-handed Weapon.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=50338/kornas-nightsavage">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Kor'nas Nightsavage</span></a> drops <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87642/darkstaff-of-annihilation">
<img alt="Darkstaff of Annihilation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_2h_pandung_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkstaff of Annihilation</span></a>, an ilvl 420 2-handed Staff.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Discipline Priests in Phase 1</span></h2>Improving your reputation with factions unlocks gear you can buy for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>. You can get reputation with all of these at once but <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> is limited so you'll want to pick your first buys carefully. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=88892/bracers-of-inlaid-jade">
<img alt="Bracers of Inlaid Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of Inlaid Jade</span></a> is quite an appealing first piece since you won't replace them until Heart of Fear raid content. Pursue Golden Lotus and Klaxxi too since both have epic items available for completing a quest once you hit Exalted.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="the-klaxxi">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_klaxxi.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> The Klaxxi</span></h3>Hitting Honored with Klaxxi also unlocks <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89230/restorative-amber">
<img alt="Restorative Amber" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_creature_amber_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Restorative Amber</span></a> which is an essential consumable in Challenge modes.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
